Yeah. Sometimes what looks like a spectrum is several choices bundled together.

Take polish the Wild Hawg bag or film the Beverage Goblin sketch. That sounds like two ends of a line. But you could shoot the sketch with the current bag and watch where people look, what they laugh at, and whether they understand what’s in the bag. Now filming gives you information about what to polish. You changed the sequence, and that created an option the original framing hid.

The same thing happens with wanting more. You can want something intensely, work hard for it, and still be okay if it takes longer than you hoped. How much you want it, how much you’ll give for it, and how much your peace depends on getting it can all move independently.

So there are two questions worth keeping together. What am I giving up if I choose this? And did I actually see the best alternative before I chose?